  {
   "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation",
   "type": "pronunciation",
   "title": "Sound changes: nasalisation",
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation_1",
     "title": "Sound changes: nasalisation",
     "summary": "Why 감사합니다 sounds like [감사함니다].",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "When ㄱ, ㄷ, ㅂ sounds meet ㄴ or ㅁ, they become nasal: ㅂ→ㅁ, ㄷ→ㄴ, ㄱ→ㅇ."
      },
      {
       "type": "table",
       "head": [
        "Spelling",
        "Pronounced",
        "Rule"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "합니다",
         "[함니다]",
         "ㅂ + ㄴ → ㅁ + ㄴ"
        ],
        [
         "거짓말",
         "[거진말]",
         "ㄷ-sound + ㅁ → ㄴ"
        ],
        [
         "한국말",
         "[한궁말]",
         "ㄱ + ㅁ → ㅇ + ㅁ"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ],
     "questions": [
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "감사합니다",
       "translation": "thank you",
       "prompt": "Say [감사함니다]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation_1_q1"
      },
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "한국말",
       "translation": "Korean language",
       "prompt": "Say [한궁말]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation_1_q2"
      },
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "입니다",
       "translation": "it is (formal)",
       "prompt": "Say [임니다]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation_1_q3"
      },
      {
       "type": "mcq",
       "prompt": "„합니다“ is pronounced:",
       "options": [
        "[함니다]",
        "[합니다] with a clear p",
        "[하니다]"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "explanation": "Nasalisation.",
       "id": "ko_l3_pronunciation_1_q4",
       "skill": "pronunciation"
      },
      {
